      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Traditionalist theologies often argue that the divine and natural law fundamentally define the procreative and unitive nature of the one-sex, lifelong, and exclusive union of a man and a woman.  They assert that changing these definitions undermines the very structure God intended for human society and the good of the family.  For them, the moral argument is that the state and the modern world are not the ultimate authority, but divine law is, and these changes represent a deviation from that inherent moral truth.",
